WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:02.201
-As the house prepares

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.069
for a formal vote to authorize

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:06.072
the impeachment inquiry
into President Trump,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.841
Republicans are comparing their
situation to a horror movie.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.043
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:15.481 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.984
Just step back and remember
that, from day one,

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.353
the actual facts
in the Ukraine scandal

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.454
have been damning
for the president.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.556
We have the notes from the call.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.891
We know that Trump held up

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.892
hundreds of millions of dollars
in military aid

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.628
that Congress had specifically
directed to Ukraine

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:31.231
and, while he was
holding up that aid,

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.866
Trump asked
the Ukrainian president

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.266
to investigate
his political rivals.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.501
It's all right there.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:38.171
Trump mentions the Bidens,
by name, multiple times.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.473
The only -- the only --
legitimate reason

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.942
a president has ever had
for mentioning Joe Biden

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.244
on a call with a foreign leader
is when Obama had

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.612
to apologize for him.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.313
[ Laughter ]
[as Obama] Uh,
Mr. Prime Minister,

00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:49.982
I'm, uh, sorry about Joe.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.984
[ Laughter ]
Just because he could see

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.453
London and France
does not mean he, uh...

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:55.889
should've anything
about your underpants.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.957
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.426
And, of course, let's not forget
that, during that phone call

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.396
with the president of Ukraine,
Trump literally said the words,

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.665
"I would like you
to do us a favor."

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.767
Remember, during the
Russia investigation,

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.269
when everyone was wondering
if there would be a smoking gun,

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.438
well, this is the smoking gun.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.674
It turns out the smoking gun was

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.809
Donald Trump's mouth
the whole time.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.911
[ Laughter ]
And his brain,

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.012
much like a revolver,

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:22.081
is only capable
of holding six words.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.717
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.087
[ Cheering and applause ]
Now, we know -- we know --

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.023
We know that one of those
words is "perfect"

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.526
because Trump keeps insisting,
every time he speaks,

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.161
almost without fail,
that his phone call

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.931
with the president of Ukraine
was not just unimpeachable,

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.064
but perfect.

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.567
He has said it dozens of times,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.035
including multiple times
just in the last week.

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:47.139
-The level of unfairness
for a perfect conversation

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.042
with the president of Ukraine.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.177
This was a perfect conversation.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.913
But this was
a perfect conversation.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.783
It's one conversation that I had

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.886
with the president of Ukraine

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.321
that was perfect.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:04.791
I had a perfect conversation
with the president of Ukraine.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.794
Perfect. The conversation
has been perfect.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.328
[ Laughter ]
I have a perfect conversation.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.664
Perfect.
The conversation was --

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.866
was perfect.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.567
[ Laughter ]
-Stop saying "perfect"!

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.702
When you overcompensate
like that,

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:18.671
it only makes you
[laughing] sound guiltier.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.807
[ Laughter ]
Most people, if you accuse them

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.809
of robbing a bank would say,
"I didn't do it."

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:23.943
Trump would say --

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.545
[as Trump]
It was a perfect transaction.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.746
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.115
I filled out the slip;
the teller was polite.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.549
Perfect.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:31.884
Perfect.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.087
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.655
Trump is just a weird,
weird man.

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:40.359
He's like an alien who learned
to mimic human behavior,

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.762
[ Laughter ]
but didn't do all the homework.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.231
Like when he was
givin' out Halloween candy

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.033
at the White House and,
for some reason,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.868
[ Laughter ]
decided to put some

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.869
on top of a kid's head.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:55.040
[ Fresh laughter ]
What's wrong with you?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.411
Are you -- Is this your first
Halloween on Earth?

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.446
[ Laughter ]
[as Trump] On my home planet,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.848
you place the candy
up on the head of the minion,

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.450
[ Laughter ]
where it waits.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.087
until all seven moons are
in alignment.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.523
If Trump's gonna do that,
he should have to put candy

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.758
on the head
[laughing] of all his minions.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.461
We're joined now by White House
Senior Advisor Stephen Miller.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.262
Is that a Hershey Kiss
on your head?

00:03:17.262 --> 00:03:18.731
[ Laughter ]
[as Miller] It is.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.933
The president put it here
and I, for one, am happy

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.701
we finally have a leader
with the courage

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.171
to put candy on the heads
of the American people.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.006
[ Laughter ]
But Trump's insistence

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.575
that the call was perfect
is actually a huge problem

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.210
for his fellow Republicans.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.278
Those Republicans are
reportedly dreading having

00:03:33.278 --> 00:03:35.448
to actually cast a vote
in the impeachment inquiry,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.516
if it gets to the Senate
because, on one hand,

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:39.118
they know what Trump did
was wrong,

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.955
but, on the other hand,
Trump won't admit it was wrong.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.255
So they have no wiggle room.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:44.624
They're basically parents

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.058
sitting in the principal's
office, saying,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.761
"I promise our son won't pull
the fire alarm again,"

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.363
while the son is sitting
next to them, saying --

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.931
[as Trump] Oh, yeah,
I'm gonna do it again.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.465
[ Laughter ]
And they have to say,

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:54.834
"He's not gonna to do it again.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.068
He's not gonna pull it.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.570
He knows what he did was wrong."
And he's saying --

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.971
[as Trump] It wasn't wrong.
It was perfect.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.407
[ Laughter ]
It was super loud

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.742
and it was super funny.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.010
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.578
And, on top of that,
Republicans are also afraid

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:08.147
of what else might come out
during the impeachment inquiry.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.448
According
to The Washington Post,

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:12.218
Republicans voiced exasperation
at the expectation

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.586
that they defend the president

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.688
against the troublesome picture
that had been painted,

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.857
with neither convincing
arguments from the White House

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.327
nor confidence that something
worse will soon be discovered.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.028
One veteran Republican
senator said,

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.363
"It feels like a horror movie."

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.398
Yeah, every minute
with Donald Trump

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:27.533
feels like a horror movie.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.134
[ Laughter ]
That's why Rudy always looks

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:31.504
like he just closed
the medicine cabinet

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.139
and saw the reflection
of the killer behind him.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:36.074
[ Laughter ]
And, I'm sorry, but you guys

00:04:36.074 --> 00:04:37.676
don't get to complain
that you're in a horror movie

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:38.878
[laughing]
when you're the ones

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.314
who invited the Babicrook
into the White House.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.282
[ Laughter ]
But Republicans were right

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.084
about one thing:
It does keep getting worse

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:49.155
as more information comes out
about the quid pro quo

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.956
Trump and his team tried
to orchestrate with Ukraine.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:54.193
For example, you might remember
that the memo from the call

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.695
that was released from the
White House specifically said

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:59.832
it was not a verbatim transcript
of the discussion,

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.568
but that didn't stop Trump
from insisting it was, anyway.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.702
-You had stenographers,

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:05.304
you had people
that took it down exactly.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.772
It was a perfect call.

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.909
All you have to read what they
wrote down, the stenographers.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.610
They wrote down an exact call.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.413
We had stenographers
on the phone,

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.148
takin' it down, word-for-word.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.451
This is an exact,
word-for-word transcript

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.353
of the conversation, right?

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:23.422
Taken by very talented
stenographers.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.491
-First of all,
they must've been talented

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.360
to make sense of what the
hell you are saying.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.561
[ Laughter ]
In fact, we know --

00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:31.997
we know it's hard to transcribe
Trump because, one time,

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.699
Trump could not say
the word "origins,"

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.635
so the White House literally had
to make up a new word,

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:39.305
spelled "oranges,"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.974
which appeared in an actual
White House transcript

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.143
because that's how Trump
kept pronouncing it.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.046
-I hope they now go and take
a look at the oranges,

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.682
[ Laughter ]
the oranges of the, uh,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.751
investigation, the beginnings.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.787
The Mueller Report,
I wish, covered

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:58.624
the oranges, how it started.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.894
-Remember when the president
of the United States

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.963
couldn't even say the word
[laughs] "origins"?

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.631
Like a college freshman

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:08.267
who accidently took too big
of a rip off a bong.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.436
[ Inhaling raspily ]

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.338
You know what's a funny word?

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.673
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:14.673
Orange-ins.

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:17.043
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.078
Orange-ins.

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:22.882
Also, it definitely seemed,
at the time,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.817
like the memo of Trump's call
was not, in fact,

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.419
a complete transcript
because there were

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:27.620
multiple ellipses throughout

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.555
and those were definitely
not pauses

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.323
because Donald Trump
does not take pauses.

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:33.893
He just yammers
until he runs out of oxygen

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.829
and then inhales like he's
about to go pearl diving.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:40.233
[ Laughter ]
[ Huffing and puffing ]

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.700
[ Fresh laughter ]
This week, we found out

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.904
that the transcript
Trump claimed was word-for-word

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:47.139
was not, in fact, word-for-word.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.942
The top Ukraine expert on the
National Security Council,

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.111
Lieutenant Colonel
Alexander Vindman,

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.413
who listened to the call,
testified on Tuesday

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:57.049
that the notes from the call
had some missing phrases

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.985
and that he tried
to correct the transcript.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.654
Now, to be clear, the phrases
do not fundamentally change

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.090
lawmakers' understanding
of the call, but nonetheless,

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:07.259
this makes clear that Vindman
is an extremely credible witness

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.127
who offered a firsthand account
of critical episodes

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:11.063
in the quid pro quo
and was so troubled

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:13.165
by Trump's July phone call
with Ukraine's president

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:15.801
that he reported his concerns
to his superior.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:17.436
The behavior was so troubling
that Trump's allies

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:18.637
can't actually defend it,
so, instead,

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:19.838
they're attacking the process

00:07:19.838 --> 00:07:21.440
and the witnesses themselves,

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.676
like Vindman,
a decorated Iraq War veteran

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:24.944
who received a Purple Heart.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.612
Trump allies in Congress
and the media have suggested

00:07:27.612 --> 00:07:29.815
that Vindman might have
an affinity towards Ukraine

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:31.850
because he emigrated from there
when he was three.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:36.689
-So, he's got a Purple Heart
and he is from the Soviet Union.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.290
He emigrated here

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.326
and has an affinity
to the Ukrainian people.

00:07:41.326 --> 00:07:42.828
We also know he was born
in the Soviet Union,

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.163
emigrated with his family,
young.

00:07:45.163 --> 00:07:48.266
He tends to feel simpatico
with the Ukraine.

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:49.836
-Simpatico? What are you,

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.437
[ Laughter ]
a right-wing beat poet?

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.639
That cat wigged out.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:56.342
Because he's simpatico,
daddy-o, you dig it?

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:59.211
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.547
Republicans can't defend
Trump's corrupt abuses of power

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:02.715
because they are indefensible.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.116
There's nothing they can say.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.218
In fact, they're so at a loss
to defend him that,

00:08:06.218 --> 00:08:07.787
even when it comes up
in private,

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.755
they quickly move on
to other topics.

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:12.491
Here's how Democratic
Senator Chris Coons explained

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:14.994
his private conversations
with Republicans in the Senate

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.062
about impeachment.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.730
-I've worked hard to develop

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.032
some meaningful friendships

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:21.567
with my Republican colleagues,

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:25.371
in order to be able to legislate
on a wide range of issues.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:28.273
We are having no
meaningful conversations

00:08:28.273 --> 00:08:30.643
-Hm.
-about what's the path forward

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:33.945
about the president's conduct
with regard to Ukraine.

00:08:33.945 --> 00:08:36.682
When I've tried to open
conversations about this,

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:38.584
my friends changed the subject.

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.519
-How do you just change
the subject?

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:41.987
Let's talk about impeachment.

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:43.522
"Speaking of peaches,
would you like some fruit?"

00:08:43.522 --> 00:08:44.856
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.856 --> 00:08:45.958
I got a bowl fulla --"

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:46.992
-Oranges.

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:50.329
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.131
Trump allies

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.932
[ Whistling ]
have run out of defenses,

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:56.234
so, now, they're just whining
about the process

00:08:56.234 --> 00:08:58.437
and smearing a witness simply
because he was alarmed

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.872
by the president's
corrupt behavior.

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:01.474
Republicans
have nothing left to say,

00:09:01.474 --> 00:09:03.442
so all they can do is
repeat Trump's lies

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:04.743
and some of them are doing it...

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:06.011
-Word-for-word.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:07.512
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:11.517
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

